<title>AUSTRALIA: RGC reports record rutile production.</title>
<headline>RGC reports record rutile production.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mineral sands and metals miner RGC Ltd said on Thursday that increased production from the U.S. state of Florida helped it achieve record rutile and ilmenite production for the year to June 30.</p>
<p>RGC detailed its latest quarterly and full year production figures for the periods ended June 30 as follows.</p>
<p>(Figures in tonnes unless otherwise stated.)  </p>
<p>RGC Mineral Sands (100 pct of output, RGC interest - 100 pct):</p>
<p>			Qtr to	Qtr to	Year to     Year to</p>
<p>		    end-Jun 97  end-Jun 96  end-Jun 97   end-Jun 96</p>
<p> Rutile		32,194     30,630     127,479	108,084</p>
<p> Synthetic Rutile  62,095     47,371     241,679	250,674</p>
<p> Ilmenite	   126,384    114,774     487,513	466,397</p>
<p> Zircon		56,246     83,278     272,265	313,103</p>
<p>Consolidated Rutile Ltd (100 pct of production, RGC interest - 39 pct from August 8, 1996):</p>
<p> Rutile		20,975     17,109	50,828	 61,333</p>
<p> Zircon		15,785     13,211	37,130	 44,926</p>
<p> Ilmenite	    47,066     52,788     165,186	190,991</p>
<p>Renison - Tin (100 pct of production, RGC interest - 100 pct):</p>
<p> Ore treated	175,841    189,849     692,248	706,425</p>
<p> Concentrates	 4,569	4,294	16,140	 16,090</p>
<p> Tin metal	    2,501	2,237	 8,637	  8,319</p>
<p>PT Koba Tin (100 pct of production, RGC interest - 75 pct):</p>
<p>Ore mined-</p>
<p> 000's cubic metres 6,746	6,193	23,361	 22,778</p>
<p> Concentrate	  3,603	3,051	12,684	 10,829</p>
<p> Tin metal	    2,474	2,232	 9,231	  4,435*</p>
<p>*Part year only, smelter commissioned December 1995  </p>
<p>Thalanga - Base Metals (100 pct of production, RGC interest - 87 pct to December 31, 1995, thereafter 100 pct):</p>
<p> Ore mined	  142,426    152,945     600,974	649,868</p>
<p> Ore milled	 140,514    163,593     600,252	652,950</p>
<p>Concentrates produced -</p>
<p> - Zinc		18,546     16,040	74,149	 77,239</p>
<p> - Copper	     4,017	5,450	18,142	 27,267</p>
<p> - Lead		 5,968	3,654	20,630	 18,737</p>
